@excelmonkey016 Recent Trendforce pricing revisions downward were for NAND, not DDR2/DDR3.

Trendforce actually still expects upward revision on legacy DRAM in 2027, despite spot prices falling in line or slightly than current prices q4.

Legacy memory is for consumers, not AI DC spend and are a different cycle than aggregate ai capex. But it’s a result of players allocating toward AI capacity reallocation, that’s happening now and continues into 2027

